ROMX $2E
	; Selectable player character. "Player Sprites" holds every overworld sheet
	; the player can be assigned (plus bike/surf) so LoadPlayerSpriteGraphics can
	; keep using a single BANK(RedSprite).
	"Player Sprites"
	"Player Appearance"
	; Displaced from banks $13 and $C by the player pics. Both are reached
	; through bank-resolving dispatch (BANK(GetPredefPointer) / jpfar), so
	; neither cares which bank it lives in.
	"Predefs"
	"Battle Engine 6"
	; Relocated from banks $03 and $1C on 2026-08-23. Both entry modules are
	; reached through bank-aware predefs and retain their internal code/data
	; clusters intact. Pin them so all three build targets agree on placement.
	"Bag Item Quantity"
	"In-Game Trades"
	; Both pinned here 2026-08-14, for the same reason: left floating, rgblink
	; first-fit drops a small section into whichever tight bank happens to have
	; room, and it can pick a DIFFERENT bank per build target. "Random" ($45
	; bytes) had landed in bank $1, taking it from $52 free to $0d. "Extra
	; Options Menu" ($67 bytes) then landed in bank $1 in the release build but
	; bank $7 in _DEBUG - and bank $7 is already one of the two that shrink most
	; under _DEBUG. Both are reached only by farcall, so BANK() resolves wherever
	; they sit. Pin small floating sections; do not trust first-fit.
	"Random"
	"Extra Options Menu"
	; Temporary Pokedex-only BG tiles. LoadPokedexTilePatterns uses BANK(), so
	; the asset is bank-independent and is pinned away from tight bank $04.
	"Pokedex Stats Bar Graphics"
	"Battle Move Info"
	"Battle Pic Helpers"
	; Yume Task 4 expands Bill's PC into a 5x4 BG-icon grid. Every exported
	; edge is bank-aware (farcall, explicit BANK(), dba, or text predef), and
	; the complete internal code/data/Cable Club cluster moves together.
	"Bill's PC"
ROMX $30
	; Species Groups Phase 2 step 4, 2026-09-08. Three species tables that each
	; MUST be one contiguous run in a single bank, because every reader indexes
	; them with a flat multiply and no bank arithmetic:
	;   BaseStats      GetMonHeader does (dex - 1) * BASE_DATA_SIZE
	;   MonsterNames   GetMonName walks NAME_LENGTH at a time
	;   CryData        GetCryData does species * 3
	; All three reach their bank via BANK(label), so they are bank-independent -
	; they just cannot be SPLIT. Their old homes ($0E, $07, $05) had 211, 6 and 9
	; bytes free respectively, i.e. all three were already out of room.
	;
	; Sizes at the full 101-species roster: BaseStats 7,056 + Monster Names 2,670
	; + Cry Data 759 = 10,485, leaving ~5,900 spare. KEEP THAT HEADROOM FREE.
	; Do NOT let a Pics section float in here - pin new Pics sections explicitly
	; (see $32 below), or a link that fits today will fail once BaseStats grows.
	"Base Stats"
	"Monster Names"
	"Pokemon Data 1"
	; Species Groups Phase 2R. MUST share this bank with "Base Stats":
	; GetMonHeader switches to BANK(BaseStats) and then plain-calls
	; ApplyFormOverride, so the two being in different banks would be a silent
	; cross-bank call into garbage. home/pokemon.asm carries a link-time ASSERT
	; that fails the build if this pin is ever dropped. Small and intentional -
	; this is NOT the kind of section the headroom warning above is about.
	"Species Forms"
ROMX $31
	; "Evos Moves" holds EvosMovesPointerTable AND the blocks it points at. Those
	; pointers are bare 16-bit `dw`, so table and data must share one bank - this
	; section can never be split the way "Pokédex Text" can. It reaches ~9,300
	; bytes at the full roster; bank $12 had FOUR bytes free.
	"Evos Moves"
ROMX $32
	; "Pokédex Text 2" is the overflow half of the dex flavour text, which passes
	; 16 KiB at the full roster. Legal to split because entries are reached by
	; bank-aware `text_far`.
	"Pokédex Text 2"
	; Species Groups Phase 2 batch 5. "Pics 7" (in $33) overflowed its bank once
	; batch 5's pics landed there; this bank had room after "Pokédex Text 2".
	"Pics 8"
	; New species pics. With BASE_PIC_BANK (step 6) a pic may live in ANY bank, so
	; these are free to go anywhere - but they are PINNED rather than floated, per
	; this file's own $2E rule, so a large pic blob cannot land in $30/$31 and eat
	; the growth headroom reserved there. The full 153-species set is ~78 KB, so
	; expect "Pics 7".."Pics N" to spill onto $33, $34 and then the mid-banks that
	; carry 4-7 KB of slack each ($15-$2D). Add each one here explicitly.
	; "Pics 6" moved OUT to bank $34 (see below) once batch 3/4's growth of
	; "Pokédex Text 2" (sharing this bank) ate the slack it depended on. Do not
	; re-add "Pics 6" here.
ROMX $33
	; AUDIO_4 - new bank added by the Shin/Yellow-style audio-engine import
	; (SHIN_IMPORT_PLAN.md Phase 1.1). All of AUDIO_4's pieces must land in
	; the same physical bank (its PlaySound/SFX headers/engine code address
	; each other bank-relatively, same as AUDIO_1/2/3 do in their own banks),
	; so - per this file's own $2E rule above - it is pinned explicitly rather
	; than left floating. $2F-$3F was entirely unallocated before this.
	"Sound Effect Headers 4"
	"Music Headers 4"
	"Sound Effects 4"
	"Audio Engine 4"
	"Music 4"
	; Species Groups Phase 2 batch 3 onward. "Pics 6" (in $32) overflowed its
	; bank once 33 species' worth of pics landed there; this bank had ~11 KB
	; free after AUDIO_4, plenty of room. Pin further "Pics N" here until this
	; bank fills too.
	"Pics 7"
ROMX $34
	; DrainHPEffect_ is entered through the existing jpfar wrapper, keeps its
	; text local, and reaches external code only through HOME/predef/far seams.
	; Pinning the intact section here creates hook room in Battle Engine 2.
	"Drain HP Effect"
	; ParalyzeEffect_ is reached by jpfar and uses only HOME/far external calls.
	"Paralyze Effect"
	; Remaining Bridge battle effects are isolated from the nearly full rogue
	; bank. Every exported entry is reached by farcall and reads no local data
	; from another bank.
	"Bridge Extended Effects"
	; Species Groups Phase 2, batches 1-2 plus the six species done ahead of
	; the batch (26 species, 52 pics, ~12.9 KB). Was floating and fit fine on
	; its own, but batch 3/4's growth elsewhere ate the slack it depended on
	; and it overflowed wherever rgblink's first-fit put it. Pinned here,
	; which had ~15.7 KB free after the existing Bridge/effect code - same
	; "pin small floating sections; do not trust first-fit" rule as "Pics 7".
	"Pics 6"
ROMX $35
	; Species Groups Phase 2R increment 7. Banks $35-$3F were entirely
	; unallocated before this (see the $2F-$3F note on bank $32 above), so the
